  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) achieves 0.653 accuracy, while the only image-only test (resnet50, singleprofile) scored a very weak 0.208. This single data point is insufficient to conclude the image modality carries no signal—resnet50 may simply be a poor encoder for this task. Uncertainty: Before investing budget in any multimodal fusion configuration, we need to know whether a stronger image encoder (ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L) can extract meaningful cellular signal. This experiment tests exactly that: image-only with ViT-L in a clean singleprofile setting, isolating the encoder choice. Why this is the best next step: If ViT-L also performs poorly, we can confidently redirect remaining budget to RNA-only optimization (e.g., exploring scgpt+multi or confirming aggregation effects). If ViT-L performs substantially better than resnet50, it justifies the next experiments in multimodal fusion with the best RNA encoder. This single experiment resolves the largest open design question—whether the image modality is worth pursuing at all—without changing multiple variables simultaneously."
}

